 ## Staging
 
-`staging-deploy.yml` finds-or-creates the `project-name-staging` D1, migrates it, and
-`wrangler deploy`s. Because previews clone this D1, staging keeps preview data and schema
-current; preview versions on the same Worker are pinned to their aliases and unaffected.
+`staging-deploy.yml` finds-or-creates the `staging` Neon branch (off the default branch),
+migrates it, and `wrangler deploy`s. Because previews branch off it, staging keeps preview
+data and schema current; preview versions on the same Worker are pinned to their aliases and
+unaffected.
 
 ## Production
 
-`prod-deploy.yml` resolves `project-name-prod` by name and **fails if it is missing** — it
-never creates it, so a misconfigured deploy cannot come up against an empty database. Locally,
-`pnpm deploy` and `pnpm db:migrate:remote` build, then use `pnpm gen:prod-config`.
+`prod-deploy.yml` resolves the Neon project's default branch and **never creates a branch**,
+so a misconfigured deploy cannot come up against an empty database. Locally, `pnpm deploy`
+builds and uses `pnpm gen:prod-config`, which needs `DB_CONNECTION_STRING` set to the
+production branch's connection string; migrate production with
+`DATABASE_URL=<url> pnpm db:migrate`.
